!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
One document, many materializations
description: file, directory, or mid-stream language switch — the concrete is not the identity
- |
  The same logical document can live in one `.yo` file, as a directory tree — each file or
  subdirectory an entry — or partly in another language: a flow token spanning several
  lines switches that subtree to json5p mid-document. A file and a subdirectory are
  equivalent ways to represent the same node, and any materialization converts to the
  others and back.
- |
  The concrete is **representation, not identity**: authored provenance the engine
  preserves, but never part of a node's identity — a reflow, a move between file and
  directory, or a language switch leaves the logical value equal. The full storage
  taxonomy is the [concretes part](::language:concretes).
